FROM cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base:latest@sha256:1c451d46a0d5c4e9f2b38e0e8d3e299564a1aa95c21973efcc1980a9d1d2e73e

# CACHEBUST busts the apk layer cache each run so daily rebuilds pick up package updates
ARG CACHEBUST=unset
# Patch ahead of upstream: relax the exact "pkg=version" pins in /etc/apk/world so
# "apk upgrade" actually applies security updates (the solver otherwise honours the
# pin and no-ops). The "=[0-9]" anchor leaves fuzzy "=~" pins alone.
USER root
RUN echo "cachebust=${CACHEBUST}" && \
    sed -i -E 's/=[0-9].*$//' /etc/apk/world && \
    apk update && apk upgrade --no-cache

USER nonroot
